    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "V1ziaB64_-LD"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Free the Fine-Tuning Artifacts and Reload the Base VLM\n"
      ],
      "id": "V1ziaB64_-LD"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CGDSwh5P_-LE"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Fine-tuning is done. Drop the optimizer state first (it is often as large as the\n",
        "# adapters themselves), then free the trainer and the 4-bit model.\n",
        "if \"trainer\" in globals() and getattr(trainer, \"optimizer\", None) is not None:\n",
        "    trainer.optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
        "    trainer.optimizer = None\n",
        "free_memory(\"trainer\", \"ft_model\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Step 9 captions every RAG image with the base VLM, so load it back now.\n",
        "model = Qwen2_5_VLForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(\n",
        "    MODEL_ID, dtype=torch.bfloat16, attn_implementation=\"sdpa\", device_map=\"auto\",\n",
        ")\n"
      ],
      "id": "CGDSwh5P_-LE"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xhPCrcyg_-LI"
      },
      "source": [
        "## <font color=\"blue\"><b>Step 9: Multimodal Dataset and Extraction</b></font>  <font color=\"red\">**[8 marks]**</font>\n"
      ],
      "id": "xhPCrcyg_-LI"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AHWuVy17_-LI"
      },
      "source": [
        "Build a small mixed-domain image corpus for the RAG pipeline: **20 CIFAR-10**,\n",
        "**20 DocVQA**, and **20 InfographicVQA** images (as in Lecture 3), each stored as a dict with\n",
        "`id`, `source`, `label`, `image`. Then extract, per image, an **EasyOCR** text pass and a\n",
        "caption (reuse `generate_with_system` with a short captioning prompt in place of Florence-2),\n",
        "and combine both into a `combined_text` field."
      ],
      "id": "AHWuVy17_-LI"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "arTuaRFx_-LJ"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "#  Step 9.1: Unified Dataset + OCR + Captions\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "CIFAR_LABELS = {0:\"airplane\",1:\"automobile\",2:\"bird\",3:\"cat\",4:\"deer\",\n",
        "                5:\"dog\",6:\"frog\",7:\"horse\",8:\"ship\",9:\"truck\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "cifar = load_dataset(\"uoft-cs/cifar10\", split=\"train[:20]\")\n",
        "infography = load_dataset(\"lmms-lab-encoder/DocVQA\", \"InfographicVQA\", split=\"validation[:20]\")\n",
        "docvqa_small = load_dataset(\"lmms-lab-encoder/DocVQA\", \"DocVQA\", split=\"validation[:20]\")\n",
        "\n",
        "RAG_DATASET = []\n",
        "## CODE HERE ##\n",
        "# Append 20 CIFAR-10 items: {\"id\", \"source\": \"cifar10\", \"label\": CIFAR_LABELS[...],\n",
        "#                            \"image\": item[\"img\"].convert(\"RGB\")}\n",
        "# Append 20 DocVQA items:   {\"id\", \"source\": \"docvqa\", \"label\": \"document\",\n",
        "#                            \"image\": item[\"image\"].convert(\"RGB\"), \"question\": item[\"question\"]}\n",
        "# Append 20 InfographicVQA items similarly with source \"infographic\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Built RAG_DATASET with {len(RAG_DATASET)} images\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ---- EasyOCR ----\n",
        "import easyocr\n",
        "ocr_reader = easyocr.Reader([\"en\"], gpu=torch.cuda.is_available(), verbose=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_ocr(image):\n",
        "    results = ocr_reader.readtext(np.array(image), detail=1, paragraph=False)\n",
        "    ## CODE HERE ##  (keep texts with confidence > 0.4, join with a space)\n",
        "    return text\n",
        "\n",
        "for item in RAG_DATASET:\n",
        "    item[\"ocr_text\"] = run_ocr(item[\"image\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "# ---- Captioning (reuse Step 5's system prompt) ----\n",
        "for item in RAG_DATASET:\n",
        "    ## CODE HERE ##\n",
        "    # item[\"caption\"] = generate_with_system(captioning_system_prompt, item[\"image\"], max_new_tokens=60)\n",
        "    pass\n",
        "\n",
        "# ---- Combine ----\n",
        "for item in RAG_DATASET:\n",
        "    ## CODE HERE ##  (item[\"combined_text\"] = caption + \" \" + ocr_text, stripped)\n",
        "    pass\n",
        "\n",
        "print(RAG_DATASET[0][\"combined_text\"])\n"
      ],
      "id": "arTuaRFx_-LJ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZBYWfiFQ_-LK"
      },
      "source": [
        "### ✍️ Step 9 Reflection  <font color=\"red\">**[2 marks]**</font>\n",
        "**[Your Answer]** must cover:\n",
        "- Why the pipeline extracts BOTH a caption and OCR text, instead of just one, giving an example image where OCR alone returns nothing. <font color=\"red\">**[1]**</font>\n",
        "- One risk of using a VLM caption to build a retrieval index (e.g. missed detail, hallucinated content). <font color=\"red\">**[1]**</font>\n"
      ],
      "id": "ZBYWfiFQ_-LK"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eoWGbVw6_-LK"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Free the Base VLM Before Loading ColPali\n"
      ],
      "id": "eoWGbVw6_-LK"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
