    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "E_A931Al_-LL"
      },
      "source": [
        "## <font color=\"blue\"><b>Step 10: Dual Retrieval: FAISS Text Index and ColPali Visual Index</b></font>  <font color=\"red\">**[12 marks]**</font>\n"
      ],
      "id": "E_A931Al_-LL"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "84vCiOxn_-LL"
      },
      "source": [
        "### <font color=\"blue\"><b>Step 10.1: Sentence Embeddings + FAISS</b></font>  <font color=\"red\">**[4 marks]**</font>\n"
      ],
      "id": "84vCiOxn_-LL"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "R02j53gD_-LL"
      },
      "source": [
        "Embed every image's `combined_text` with `all-mpnet-base-v2`, build a FAISS\n",
        "`IndexFlatIP` (cosine similarity via normalised inner product), and write a `text_retrieve`\n",
        "function. Sanity-check it with a text query."
      ],
      "id": "R02j53gD_-LL"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rhaoU1UW_-LM"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "#  Step 10.1: FAISS Text Retrieval\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "import faiss\n",
        "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n",
        "\n",
        "st_model = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2\", device=DEVICE)\n",
        "\n",
        "combined_texts = [item[\"combined_text\"] for item in RAG_DATASET]\n",
        "## CODE HERE ##\n",
        "# text_embeddings = st_model.encode(..., normalize_embeddings=True, convert_to_numpy=True).astype(\"float32\")\n",
        "\n",
        "dim = text_embeddings.shape[1]\n",
        "## CODE HERE ##  (build faiss.IndexFlatIP(dim) and add text_embeddings)\n",
        "\n",
        "def text_retrieve(query, top_k=5):\n",
        "    ## CODE HERE ##\n",
        "    # encode the query the same way, search the index, return list of (idx, score)\n",
        "    return list(zip(indices[0].tolist(), scores[0].tolist()))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(text_retrieve(\"a fluffy pet animal\", top_k=5))\n"
      ],
      "id": "rhaoU1UW_-LM"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "x6x9sh9K_-LN"
      },
      "source": [
        "### <font color=\"blue\"><b>Step 10.2: ColPali Visual Index</b></font>  <font color=\"red\">**[4 marks]**</font>\n"
      ],
      "id": "x6x9sh9K_-LN"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "WBCghGQ1_-LN"
      },
      "source": [
        "Load `vidore/colpali-v1.3`, embed every image as a set of patch vectors, and write\n",
        "`colpali_retrieve` using **MaxSim** late interaction. Visualise the MaxSim relevance as a\n",
        "heatmap over one retrieved image's patches."
      ],
      "id": "WBCghGQ1_-LN"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "t-oQys_y_-LO"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "#  Step 10.2: ColPali Visual Retrieval\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "from colpali_engine.models import ColPali, ColPaliProcessor\n",
        "\n",
        "colpali_model = ColPali.from_pretrained(\"vidore/colpali-v1.3\", dtype=torch.bfloat16, device_map=\"cuda:0\")\n",
        "colpali_proc = ColPaliProcessor.from_pretrained(\"vidore/colpali-v1.3\")\n",
        "colpali_model.eval()\n",
        "\n",
        "def embed_images_colpali(images, batch_size=2):\n",
        "    all_embs = []\n",
        "    ## CODE HERE ##\n",
        "    # For each batch: colpali_proc.process_images(batch) -> move tensors to GPU ->\n",
        "    # torch.inference_mode(): colpali_model(**inputs) -> move to CPU, append per-image tensors\n",
        "    return all_embs\n",
        "\n",
        "colpali_image_embeddings = embed_images_colpali([item[\"image\"] for item in RAG_DATASET])\n",
        "\n",
        "def colpali_retrieve(query, top_k=5):\n",
        "    ## CODE HERE ##\n",
        "    # 1. colpali_proc.process_queries([query]) -> GPU -> colpali_model(**inputs)[0] -> CPU\n",
        "    # 2. MaxSim(query_emb, image_emb) for every image: (query_emb @ image_emb.T).max(dim=1).values.sum()\n",
        "    # 3. sort descending, return top_k (idx, score) pairs\n",
        "    return results\n",
        "\n",
        "print(colpali_retrieve(\"a fluffy pet animal\", top_k=5))\n"
      ],
      "id": "t-oQys_y_-LO"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pH22JuEI_-LP"
      },
      "source": [
        "### ✍️ Step 10 Reflection  <font color=\"red\">**[4 marks]**</font>\n",
        "**[Your Answer]** must cover:\n",
        "- Why cosine similarity is achieved here by inner product on normalised vectors, and what `IndexFlatIP` computes. <font color=\"red\">**[1]**</font>\n",
        "- What MaxSim does conceptually (per query-token best-matching patch, summed) and why it can catch detail that captions/OCR miss. <font color=\"red\">**[2]**</font>\n",
